~ start
set voice_pitch = 0.25
Mayor: Well, well, well...
Mayor: If it ain't my little garbage man.
Mayor: I see you've stumbled upon my dirty little secret.
Mayor: Yes, it was me who stole that piece of the ancient shrine.
Mayor: Support from my constituents has been lackluster as of late.
Mayor: They're "[wave]concerned[/wave]" that my policies regarding pterosaurs are "[wave]discriminatory[/wave]".
Mayor: The fools. My policies are [wave]far[/wave] too lenient. 
Mayor: Those filthy pteros are invadin' this city and turnin' it into a crime ridden mess. 
Mayor: I needed funds, and the dinos of this city needed their eyes opened.
Mayor: That's why I stole this priceless artifact, and why I had that quetzal thrown in jail.
Mayor: He will serve as the cornerstone of my re-election. A powerful reminder of the nature of pterosaurs.
Mayor: But now you've gone and thrown a wrench into my machinations...
Mayor: It's a shame, I hate to lose a hardworkin' dino such as yourself due to a little slip up like this.
Mayor: But I can't let you leave now that you've seen this.
=> END